# GENERATED FILE -- do not edit.
#
# Rendered from upstream.conf.tmpl by ops/nginx/render-upstream.sh, which reads
# the active slot from /srv/voting/state/active-slot. That file is the single
# source of truth for which release is serving. An edit made here will work until
# the next deploy replaces this file, which is the worst kind of change: one that
# appears to succeed and then quietly reverts.
#
# Exactly one server is listed, deliberately.
#
# The obvious alternative -- listing both slots and letting nginx balance between
# them -- cannot express "only send traffic to the new version after it has
# passed its health check". Passive balancing has no notion of readiness, so it
# would start sending live traffic to a slot the moment it starts, which is
# precisely the window that produces 5xx during a deploy. Switching the upstream
# by rewriting this file is what keeps the health gate authoritative.
#
# max_fails/fail_timeout: if the active slot stops answering, nginx stops sending
# to it for 10s rather than piling up requests against a dead backend. This is a
# backstop for the case where a slot dies between deploys, not part of the deploy
# mechanism -- the health gate is what decides when traffic moves.
#
# keepalive 32 matches the `proxy_http_version 1.1` and `Connection ""` headers
# in 10-app.conf. Without all three, nginx opens a new upstream connection per
# request and the setting does nothing.

upstream voting_app {
    server ${ACTIVE_SLOT}:3000 max_fails=3 fail_timeout=10s;
    keepalive 32;
}
